  "instance_name": "disgusting_pig_mapping",
  "label": "The wild boar is mapped as 'disgusting' entity requiring legal protection from hatred",
  "description": "The text 'imagine being so disgusting there have to be laws to try to stop normal people from hating you' directly maps the visual entity 'wild_boar' as the embodiment of 'disgusting' — an entity so repulsive that it necessitates legal protection from hatred. This is a dehumanizing metaphor where the animal is used to represent humans perceived as 'disgusting' or 'unacceptable'. The mapping is explicit through the text's juxtaposition with the visual of the muddy, dirty boar, reinforcing the stereotype that such beings are inherently 'dirty' and thus deserving of legal protection from social rejection.",
